A run is stopped as a terminal would stop it, SIGINT to its process
group.
In a jail
.Pq the job's jail, the read's host-jail
poudriere is the jail's own, run there by
.Xr jexec 8 ,
its build jails the jail's children: its files are read and written
beneath the jail's root, never through a link out of it, its runs kept
on the host as
.Pa builder/jails/ Ns Ar jail Ns Pa / Ns Ar n .
A jail without what poudriere needs there is refused with what to set
in its
.Xr jail.conf 5 :
.Va children.max
above 0,
