the probes (arcana-probe): each edge's SD-WAN targets with the
interfaces whose links it watches, and the admin's monitors on any
tunnel, the host's and each vnet jail edge's, set together an edge and
a kind at a time, kept beside the history file for the next start
.Pq Pa sdwan-probes.json , monitors.json , No and their Pa @ Ns Ar jail No files ;
a monitor without an address, on the host, probes its interface's far
end through the interface's FIB.
How a target is measured is its kind, arcana-probe's:
.Cm icmp ,
pinged alone (the console's breakout beacons);
.Cm stamp ,
by STAMP alone, with no fallback and no raw socket (so without root
too): a reflector silent, refusing or unkeyed makes it down, why told
in its session; refused at a jail's edge;
.Cm auto ,
the default, by STAMP when it is Arcana's far end (an SD-WAN target of
the host's), ICMP its fallback.
What STAMP sees of each is arcana-stamp's state, a session a target
(the reflector and its mode, the last reply's delay each way, the DSCP
each way, the NAT, authenticated, the counters all along), with the
sender's settings and
.Xr stampd 8
as the agent sets it.
A target measured by STAMP is measured
through
.Xr libstamp 3 Ns 's
sender, a UDP socket in the target's FIB
.Pq Dv SO_SETFIB ,
receive times by
.Dv SO_TS_MONOTONIC :
the round trip with the reflector's time taken out; the delay each way,
the packets carrying the Timestamp Information TLV (RFC 8972), one way
(T2 \- T1 and T4 \- T3 on the time of day) when both ends' error
estimates say their clocks are synchronised
.Pq Xr ntp_gettime 2 , No or Fl -stamp-clock
and the two errors together are no more than a tenth of half the round
trip, else half the round trip, flagged an estimate; the DSCP each way,
the Class of Service TLV asking the reflector to reply with the
target's DSCP and telling the DSCP the probe reached it with, the
reply's read as it comes
.Pq Dv IP_RECVTOS , IPV6_RECVTCLASS ,
so that a DSCP rewritten on the way, or one the reflector refuses, is
seen; the addresses and ports the far end saw, the Location TLV, a NAT
on the way told (the source not the socket's own, the destination not
the target's); and, the
reflector being stateful, the loss on the way out told from the loss on
the way back, by its sequence numbers and by the Direct Measurement
TLV's counters (the packets sent, those the reflector received and
sent back); the others, the monitors and a jail edge's targets are pinged
.Pq ICMP echo .
Under
.Cm auto ,
a far end whose STAMP port is refused, or that answers none of as many
STAMP probes as would make the target down, is pinged instead, the
first echo deciding whether the tunnel is down; STAMP is tried every
ten seconds and taken up again when it answers.
A plain tunnel's target (GRE, gif or geneve that neither IPsec nor
WireGuard protects) is measured in STAMP's authenticated mode (RFC 8762
section 4.4, HMAC-SHA-256 truncated to 128 bits): the console names
this end's tunnel and the far end's public half of its pair, and the
key and SSID are derived from the tunnel's X25519 pair
(its key-pair entry of the IKE-less lists, arcana-ikeless)
and that half by HKDF-SHA256, the same at both ends, never sent nor
known to the console; a reply that does not authenticate is no reply,
so a far end of another key, or a probe tampered with on the way,
falls back to ICMP as an unanswered reflector does.
Fallen back, such a target is measured by what nothing authenticates,
which one on the path can force: it raises the alarm
.Cm stamp-unauthenticated
(Warning, saying why), cleared when authenticated STAMP answers again.
A key that brings no authenticated answer is derived anew at each
STAMP try (under
.Cm stamp ,
every ten seconds while the target is down), so a pair made again at
this end is used without the console; the far end's new half comes
only with the console's next apply.
Each such key is written, in place and 0600, after Arcana's marker in
.Xr stampd 8 Ns 's
key file
.Pq Fl -stampd-keys ,
the admin's lines before it kept, and stampd told (restarted when the
file is new to it); no key is logged.
The far end of a measurement is
.Xr stampd 8 ,
the STAMP reflector Arcana installs, one a FIB: the agent sets
.Va stampd_enable
and
.Va stampd_fibs ,
the FIBs of the host's probe targets and steered routes, as it writes
the rest of
.Xr rc.conf 5
(Arcana's file or the admin's, by config-files);
.Va stampd_fibs
is a word list: Arcana's FIBs are added after the admin's, and only its
own are taken out; it runs
.Ql service stampd reload ,
which starts it in a FIB added, stops it in one gone and tells the
others; with no such FIB, what it set is taken out and stampd stopped.
A refusal (rc-conf-files not accepted, a value of the admin's in the
way) is logged once and tried again a minute later or at the next
change; nothing is set while stampd's rc script is not installed;
.It
